WHAT: Folds phi nodes that merge constants 0 and 1 from conditional
branches into the branch condition itself (or its negation).

WHY: Fe generates patterns like 'if cond { true } else { false }' which
lower to a branch + phi selecting between 0 and 1. This fold recognizes
the pattern and replaces the phi with the condition directly.

GAS IMPACT: None on rosetta contracts. Fe's bool handling was already
improved in earlier compiler work (Ne instead of double-negation).

TEAM NOTES: Another correct-but-inapplicable optimization. The pattern
would help if Fe still generated redundant bool round-trips, but that
was already fixed at the Fe level.
